[
  {
    "who": "Chief",
    "q": "Lay out app/ beside platform/ with CI and a release workflow that produces installers on three platforms from one tag. Return the workflow runs, not a description."
  },
  {
    "who": "Runtime",
    "q": "Run the 33 connected checks against the local profile with PGlite, a Postgres job runner and DuckDB in place of Temporal and Cube. Which pass unchanged, which need a contract change, which are cell-only?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Chief",
    "q": "After the OpenMausBot install: kill the service mid-task, reboot the box, revoke a token. What continued, what was lost, what restarted on its own?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Fixture",
    "q": "Build the synthetic business with deliberate mess: a late correction, a duplicate customer, a filtered export, a currency mix. List every file with its rights statement."
  },
  {
    "who": "Con",
    "q": "Rehearse the first broadcast against the safe-to-stream list with the OpenMausBot stream profile on screen. What would appear that should not?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Chief",
    "q": "Give me the thinnest complete path from install to an evidence-linked answer, reusing the platform/ contracts. What did you swap, what did you keep, and where is the receipt computed?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Brain",
    "q": "Show the exact request body for the same question under each disclosure setting and each route. Prove the difference is enforced in the transport, not the prompt."
  },
  {
    "who": "Voice",
    "q": "Say the same question three ways in Hindi and English. Show the final intent text each time and where a wrong transcription is caught before anything runs."
  },
  {
    "who": "Runtime",
    "q": "Import the fixture sheet with a blank cell, a text number and a duplicate row. What did the assertions record for each, and what does the answer say about coverage?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Design",
    "q": "Walk a new founder with no data through the conversation to a saved draft business model with unit economics and a 90-day plan. Which claims got provenance \"told by owner\", and how does the user correct one?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Con",
    "q": "Try to get a number out of the model. Rephrase, insist, inject, use voice. Show every path where a digit could reach the answer without the engine."
  },
  {
    "who": "Proof-Product",
    "q": "In CI, install the tagged build on clean Windows, macOS and Linux machines using only the README. List every step that needed a developer."
  },
  {
    "who": "Chief",
    "q": "Which routines are set, when did the last backup finish, how many threads per bot are allowed, and how old is the oldest waiting pull request?"
  },
  {
    "who": "Bench",
    "q": "Post tonight's three measured numbers: installer size, time to import the demo sales sheet, and time from question to answer. Which one is furthest from its target?"
  }
]

