      "w": "do",
      "do": "Open the Build room. Paste:",
      "prompt": "Forge, start block 1 with Ledger and Design: people, machines and sign-in for a local app. Start from docs/identity.md, written on day 1, and extend it into docs/seats-and-devices.md first, in plain words. Principals are of three kinds: person, device, agent. Each person signs in on a machine with their own passphrase; there is no server account. Each machine creates its own key pair at install; the private key is wrapped by the OS keychain and by the passphrase of the person. The workspace key is wrapped once for each admitted device public key. Invite flow: the new machine shows a short verification code, the owner compares it and approves on a machine that is already in; an invite is single use and expires after 15 minutes. An agent started by a person gets the same or fewer permissions than that person, never more. Design builds the seats list and the machines list in the trust panel. Fixture provides three made-up people for the demo workspace: Meera Demo (cofounder), Anil Demo (accountant) and a demo CA. Post the plan in five lines with the branch name, then start. Report as Changed / Verified / Partial / Needs."
    },
    {
      "w": "off",
      "do": "The invites happen off camera, in the private step at 2:35, once Ledger reports that the invite works: the made-up cofounder and the made-up accountant on machine two, and Moheek from his own machine, in a separate test workspace that is never on screen. Invite codes never go on screen, even the demo ones. Moheek's face, email and screen never appear."
    },
