The paid plan promises jobs that run while the laptop is closed. Today we write down how that must work, and what it costs in privacy. A server cannot use your own command-line login, so it needs an API key or the Chausar allowance. To do the work it must read the data you send it, so that part cannot be end-to-end encrypted. It is built after day 10.

