{
  "id": "main",
  "title": "The order for Chief",
  "room": "Build room",
  "goal": "Give the companion hands, and prove they can be trusted. Every action comes from a written catalogue, follows five steps, and is read back from the real system. Then the companion sets up its own scheduled jobs, with limits, a catch-up rule for a laptop that was asleep, and a background mode. Use test targets only: my test mailbox, the test sheet and the Zoho Books trial organisation. Start from your morning report: anything still partial from day 6 comes first.",
  "first": "Post the name of the local job runner library chosen on day 1 and its test list (crash, double start, lost reply), so the drills of today run on the real runner and not on a stand-in.",
  "private": [
    "Give write permission to the three test targets inside Chausar: the test mailbox, the test sheet and the Zoho Books trial organisation. Reading was allowed on earlier days. Writing is a separate permission. I do this off camera.",
    "If a second Zoho trial organisation exists, its sign-in goes to Con only."
  ],
  "lanes": [
    {
      "who": "Ledger with Pipeline and Design",
      "detail": "Block 1. The action catalogue: one typed row per action per system with its effect class, approval rule, validity window, idempotency rule, read-back method and status. The phrase \"everything Codex can do\" is removed everywhere. Anything not in the catalogue returns \"not in my list yet\". Design builds the catalogue table in the trust panel."
    },
    {
      "who": "Runtime with Ledger",
      "detail": "Blocks 2 and 3. The five steps on the day 1 job runner with one operation id: prepare, approve, do, read back, settle. Approvals bind the exact request and expire. An unknown result is a real state, settled by read-back, never by a blind retry. A would-have-done column in the ledger for day 8."
    },
    {
      "who": "Core with Mapper-1 and Proof-Connectors",
      "detail": "Block 4. Write-back recipes: an outbound block in the mapping language and the compiler, recipes for the test sheet and the Zoho Books trial organisation, and a write-back test that runs apart from the read tests. A read recipe never implies a write recipe."
    },
    {
      "who": "Ledger with Design and Brain",
      "detail": "Block 5. Approval tiers: a grouped approval for internal actions that can be undone; one approval each for money, outside messages, deleting and anything that cannot be undone; statutory filings are prepare only for good. A slow-down notice when approvals look blind."
    },
    {
      "who": "Pipeline with Voice, Analyst and Munim",
      "detail": "Blocks 6 and 7. The collections loop on test targets: opt-in, caps and stop word, a reminder with the invoice link, sent once, read back, and paid as a separate later fact. Then a bill photo to a booked entry in the Zoho trial organisation, experimental."
    },
    {
      "who": "Runtime with Forge, Design and Analyst",
      "detail": "Blocks 8 and 9. The scheduled jobs the companion sets up, with limits: no job creates a job without approval, a cap on active jobs, a failing job is set aside. Each step is marked as needing a model or not. The missed-run rule, the catch-up sweep on wake, and background mode with a tray icon."
    },
    {
      "who": "Runtime with Ops and Ledger",
      "detail": "Block 10. The drills: kill in the middle of a send, power cut, restore an older backup. On restore, sending is blocked until every action in the gap has been read back and the deletion list has been applied again."
    },
    {
      "who": "Atlas with Runtime, Brain and Warden",
      "detail": "Block 11. The one-page architecture note for paid always-on jobs, in plain words, with its limits. Overnight, Runtime tries the runner with no screen on a second machine, as the home box experiment."
    },
    {
      "who": "Con, Warden and Bench",
      "detail": "Block 12. Con writes and runs the attack cases for actions and jobs and holds the hidden ones. Warden checks that no agent can read a token, a password or a portal sign-in. Bench adds the open action cases to the test bench and posts the score on every build."
    },
    {
      "who": "Mapper-1 with Lens and Corpus",
      "detail": "The learning log. Every write-back decision and every read-back result is written to the log in the day 1 event format: structure only, no values, names or amounts. Sharing stays off by default."
    },
    {
      "who": "Factory, always on (Corpus, the nine Scouts, Mapper-2, Mapper-3, Proof-Connectors, Lens)",
      "detail": "The factory keeps running on the 50 systems. New today: each dossier gets its write-back lines for the catalogue: what the documents of the vendor say about duplicate requests, which reference can be searched, and the retry window. Where the documents say nothing, write \"unknown result, ask the user\". Report any change to the four counts (researched, sampled, mapped, qualified)."
    },
    {
      "who": "Muse and Atlas",
      "detail": "Muse: the daily recap and the clip list. Atlas: docs/actions-catalogue.md, docs/write-back-recipes.md and docs/jobs.md as the builders write them."
    }
  ],
  "done": [
    "The action catalogue is in the repository and in the app, and a search for the old phrase finds nothing.",
    "A lost reply caused no second send: the ledger run shows not sure yet, then sent once.",
    "Every live action has a ledger record with all five steps under one number.",
    "An approval was cancelled by a changed amount, by its expiry and by an undone merge: three log lines.",
    "The write-back recipes for the test sheet and Zoho pass their own test run, with a score apart from the read score.",
    "A reminder without consent was blocked, and the daily cap held.",
    "The reminder loop shows sent and paid as two journal entries.",
    "The job the companion proposed was created, paused and deleted, and a job that tried to create a job waited for a yes.",
    "After sleep the missed job ran once, and the brief lists it.",
    "The drill log shows no second send after a crash and a restore, and the deleted item is still deleted.",
    "The always-on note is merged, with the review by Warden.",
    "The attack cases for actions are in the test bench, and the score for today is posted."
  ]
}

