A job stops when the laptop is closed, unless another machine runs it. There are two ways. A home box is a spare laptop or a mini PC at the shop that runs the same engine. The paid service runs the job on our server. We say one thing plainly: a server that runs your job must hold a key to your data, so it is not the same promise as a backup we cannot read.

