{
  "what": "No new features after the day 9 tag. One exact build, called the release candidate, is tested all day, and that same build is the one we sign. If the certificate has not arrived, we ship a clearly labelled preview with a fingerprint anyone can check.",
  "piece": "release",
  "architectureNodes": "tag=Day 9 tag, plus fixes only;rc=Release candidate: one exact build;you=You sign it, no bot holds the key|fp=Fingerprint published beside the download;win=Windows: signed and supported|other=Mac and Linux: labelled previews|no=No certificate yet: a preview with a plain warning",
  "architectureEdges": "tag>rc;rc>you;rc>fp;you>win;you>other;you>~no",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "w": "say",
      "say": "Today nothing new gets built. The build is frozen at last night's tag, and only fixes go in. One exact build is tested all day. That same build is the one we sign. Signing is a publisher's stamp. It tells Windows that this file really comes from us. One honest note: even a signed app from a new publisher can show a Windows warning for some weeks. So we also publish a fingerprint of the file, and anyone can check it."
    },
    {
